   <standOff><listPerson><person xml:id="person3892"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa skya paN+Di ta kun dga' rgyal mtshan</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ས་སྐྱ་པཎྜི་ཏ་ཀུན་དགའ་རྒྱལ་མཚན</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa skya paṇḍita</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos rje sa paN</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs gter gangs can mkhas pa'i gtsug rgyan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa paN</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa skya lo tsA ba</persName><birth notBefore="1182-01-01" notAfter="1182-12-31">1182</birth><death notBefore="1251-01-01" notAfter="1251-12-31">1251</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1056</idno><idno type="APIS">3892</idno><note type="comment">See [8S7FDMCJ]: 107 for a list of his most important disciples.</note></person><person xml:id="person5910"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sangs rgyas rgyal mtshan</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">སངས་རྒྱས་རྒྱལ་མཚན</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gsang phu'i gdan rabs sum cu pa sangs rgyas rgyal mtshan</persName><birth notBefore="1200-01-01">after 1200</birth><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">5910</idno><note type="comment">Scholar writing after 1219 as he quotes the Tshad ma rigs gter (ID:5564) in his epistemological work (ID:4772).&#13;
According to [8H6M69W4], he was the 13th abbot of gSang phu. He could be identical to (ID:6301), the 24th abbot of the lower monastery of gSang phu (ID:6158) active in the middle of the 14th century. See [J4L5X9AG]: 432, n. 56.</note></person><person xml:id="person5911"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mdar btsun pa rin chen bzang po</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">མདར་བཙུན་པ་རིན་ཆེན་བཟང་པོ</persName><birth notBefore="1250-01-01">after 1250</birth><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">5911</idno><note type="comment">[J4L5X9AG]: 432, n. 56 suggests that he could be identical with bSam gtan bzang po (ID:6127), the abbot of the lower monastery of gSang phu (ID:6158) preceding Sangs rgyas rgyal mtshan ([MPRU5QUC]: 201, sMad 23). However, their names do not completely match.</note></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work4773"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma'i mtshan nyid bsdus pa rigs pa'i sgo 'byed pa</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཚད་མའི་མཚན་ཉིད་བསྡུས་པ་རིགས་པའི་སྒོ་འབྱེད་པ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma'i mtshan nyid rigs pa'i sgo 'byed</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1219-01-01">after 1219</date><author ref="person:5910">sangs rgyas rgyal mtshan</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">The work was composed after 1219 as it cites the Tshad ma rigs gter (ID: 5564), and possibly after 1300 as it refers to Mokṣākaragupta (ID:5556). If its place of composition, dBen gnas Brag dkar, refers to Brag dkar rta so, it was composed after 1525.&#13;
&#13;
The presentation is a compilation of definitions and typologies organized in 20 topics (which reminds one of the "lessons" in bsdus grwa compositions), which are the same as in work (ID:4767) by Byang chub sems dpa' dz+nya na shrI (ID:4017). See [J4L5X9AG]: 435.&#13;
The author only presents his own system and does not confront his views with those of other thinkers. The work contains numerous citations from Indian sources.</note><relatedItem type="citesWork" target="work:5564"/><respStmt><resp>prompter</resp><name ref="person:5911">mdar btsun pa rin chen bzang po</name></respStmt><idno type="APIS">4773</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5564"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rigs gter</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཚད་མ་རིགས་གཏེར</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1219-01-01" notAfter="1219-12-31">1219</date><author ref="person:3892">sa skya paN+Di ta kun dga' rgyal mtshan</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">On 1219 as the approximate date of composition, see [8S7FDMCJ]: 101 and 303, n. 293.</note><idno type="APIS">5564</idno></bibl></listBibl><listPlace><place xml:id="place5697"><placeName xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brag dkar</placeName><placeName xml:lang="bo">བྲག་དཀར</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">dben gnas brag dkar</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">brag dkar rta so</placeName><location><geo>28.612917 85.259444</geo></location><idno type="APIS">5697</idno></place></listPlace><listRelation><relation xml:id="rel2324" name="requests" active="#person5911" passive="#person5910" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex45022023-09-19"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel2323" name="active-at" active="#person5910" passive="#place5697" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex45022023-09-19"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel4947" name="quotes-without-name" active="#person5910" passive="#person3892" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex45022024-09-1110-23-42"/><ptr target="#ex45022024-09-1110-23-422"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel743" name="author-of" active="#person5910" passive="#work4773" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex45022023-09-19"/></desc></relation><relation xml